WEBVTT

00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:13,870
I have just begun taking 10,000 I use a vitamin D daily.

00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:19,150
Last, I had a check, but two months ago, my level was 55.

00:00:19,150 --> 00:00:22,750
I live in Iowa and I'm getting virtually no sunshine.

00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:26,670
How often should I get my level checked?

00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:33,070
Well, if your vitamin D level is 55, that is certainly not high.

00:00:33,070 --> 00:00:39,070
So on taking 10,000 a day, is that dangerous?

00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,870
None of your vitamin D level is 55.

00:00:41,870 --> 00:00:46,990
If your vitamin D level was 155 in your taking 10,000 a day,

00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:51,230
I'd be the first to tell you to decrease your dosage.

00:00:51,230 --> 00:00:55,550
There's nothing wrong with 155 vitamin D level.

00:00:55,550 --> 00:01:00,350
Still, I think there's any danger in that, but you certainly don't need to be taking 10,000.

00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:04,510
So when should you get your vitamin D level checked again?

00:01:04,510 --> 00:01:08,990
If two months ago, it was 55 and you just started taking 10,000,

00:01:08,990 --> 00:01:10,590
or I would say a couple months.

00:01:11,390 --> 00:01:17,550
However, I would say you probably should be getting blood work more often than that.

00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:24,430
So if they're going to do blood work to test CBC levels and complete metabolic panel,

00:01:24,430 --> 00:01:26,430
why not ask for a vitamin D level?

00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:31,790
I mean, literally it's $3 and up to that test.

00:01:31,790 --> 00:01:39,390
So every time you get blood work, just ask for a vitamin D level.

